cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "less_slow.py: Less Slow Coding Practices in Python, from Numerics & NumPy to Generators, Async IO, & Networking"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.2
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/less_slow.py
url: https://ashvardanian.com/tags/less-slow/
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21626661
abstract: >-
  Educational micro-benchmarks for building a performance-first mindset in
  Python, measuring the real cost of abstractions from a few nanoseconds
  upward. It spans numerics and matrix decompositions with NumPy and Numba,
  Unicode and string handling, callbacks, generators, iterators, and async
  generators, polymorphism and dynamic dispatch, composite structures from
  dictionaries and dataclasses to NamedTuples, attrs, and Pydantic models,
  heterogeneous data with Pandas and Arrow, control flow and micro-patterns,
  memory, garbage collection, and allocation behavior, error handling with
  exceptions versus status codes, reflection and dynamic code generation,
  plus networking with sockets, HTTPX, FastAPI, and Uvicorn.

authors:
